"The System offers access to about 0.07% of people; they are called or chosen."
"Most are chosen between the ages of 15 and 17."
"About 70% are chosen after their 16th birthday and before their 17th."
"S- and A-ranks are disproportionately chosen at 15; D- and F-ranks at 17."
"Children of superhumans are much more likely to be chosen."
"Selection feels like a brief, painless full-body spasm, like a hypnic jerk."
"The System then gives its selection speech aloud, almost never as text."
"Theory holds the System reads the selectee's reactions and tweaks mind or soul as it merges."
"Selection ends a guardian's legal guardianship; the selectee is no longer a citizen."
"Until they accept, selectees have no powers affixed and feel wholly human."
"The System picks most children of Avowed and almost never anyone else."
"On selection U.S. citizenship expires with an exit letter pledging service to all known peoples."
"Everyone knows the selection speech by heart; it cites the 1963 agreement with the Artonans."
"Class is randomly assigned based on the Artonan Triplanetary Government's current requests."
"An S at seventeen is almost as odd as an F at fifteen; the System picks powerful people younger."
"The System hates outliers; only a few people each year are selected before fifteen."
"Children of two non-Avowed are rarely selected; every globie is a statistical miracle."
"Avowed of the same rank vary in foundation points, stats, extra impressions and affixation offers."
"Selectees show a floating name tag of their choosing and a non-Avowed notice."
"Siblings of globie Avowed are selected much more often than the general population."
